    {
      "content": "When retiring a routing mechanism that resolves to a DIFFERENT AGENT per effort mode (e.g. a '-hard'-suffixed agent-level ladder rung) in favor of one that injects CONTRACT TEXT into the same agent's dispatch prompt, land the new injection mechanism and demonstrate it per domain BEFORE removing the old resolution rung. Removing the old rung first silently downgrades every affected dispatch to a contract-free standard agent with no visible error -- the two mechanisms are easy to conflate (both gate on --hard) but resolve fundamentally different things (an agent name vs. a list of contract file paths), so there is no natural 'it still works' signal to catch a misorder.",
