    {
      "content": "This agent-system's deploy copier is additive-only: deleting or renaming a source-store file never removes its stale counterpart from an already-deployed tree (.claude/**). After every source-store rename/deletion plus redeploy, run gate 13 (whole-tree orphan detection) and expect it to surface exactly these stale artifacts -- both orphan FILES (the old deployed path still on disk) and GHOST INDEX ROWS (a stale entry in the merged .claude/context/index.json pointing at a path whose source row no longer exists). Both must be removed manually; this is documented, deliberate behavior (deploy-orphan-detection.md's 'detect, never auto-delete' design), not a bug to route around.",
      "category": "PATTERN",
